### Deployment
- **Vercel**: Connected to GitHub repo. Auto-deploys on push.
- **Node version**: Set via `NODE_VERSION` env var in Vercel.
- **Framework override**: Must NOT be set to null (breaks Git-triggered builds).
- **Build cache**: Must clear `.angular/cache` before build (`rm -rf .angular/cache` in `vercel.json`). Stale cache caused auth routes to be missing in production.
- **CDN headers**: HTML responses must include `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate` to prevent stale `index.html` serving.
- **Edge Functions**: Weather proxy at `api/weather.ts` with 15-minute edge caching. Deepgram ephemeral-token mint at `api/deepgram-token.ts` (no caching, ~30s TTL tokens).

### Voice Input (Deepgram)
- **STT provider**: Deepgram Nova-3 over WebSocket streaming.
- **Auth**: Ephemeral access tokens via `POST https://api.deepgram.com/v1/auth/grant`. Master `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY` lives only in Vercel + local `.env`; never exposed to the browser.
- **Master key role**: Must be **Member** or higher on the Deepgram project, otherwise `auth/grant` returns `403 Forbidden: Insufficient permissions` and the mic appears to do nothing. Read-only and project-scoped keys are insufficient.
- **Browser handshake**: Use `@deepgram/sdk` (5.1+), not raw `new WebSocket(url)`. The SDK converts `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` into `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: bearer, <jwt>` (browsers cannot set custom headers).
- **SDK v5 string-boolean params**: `interim_results`, `smart_format`, `punctuate` ConnectArgs must be `'true'`/`'false'` strings. Booleans compile under `tsc` but `ng build`'s template type-check refuses them.
- **Vocabulary tier**: Tier 2 keyterm prompting. Static glossary (~120 construction/Trimble terms) + dynamic project + persona names via `buildVoiceKeyterms(dataStore)`. Cap at ~150 entries to keep WebSocket URL length safe.
- **Cleanup contract**: Five resources released through one idempotent path -- MediaStream tracks, MediaRecorder, AudioContext, WebSocket (CloseStream then close), rAF callback. Six stop hooks: Send (button + Enter), Escape, `controller.thinking()` effect, `visibilitychange: hidden`, `DestroyRef.onDestroy`, mic toggle.
- **Performance**: Audio level meter rAF runs `runOutsideAngular`, writes directly to `--mic-level` CSS variable on `documentElement`. No template binds the level signal -- avoiding 60fps change detection across the app.
- **Dual-implementation rule**: Every `/api/*` endpoint must exist BOTH in `api/<name>.ts` (Vercel Edge runtime) AND `dev-proxy.mjs` handler routed at `localhost:3001`, otherwise `npm start` 404s the endpoint. See skill section 45.

## Known Fragile Areas

These areas have broken multiple times. Extra care required:

| Area | Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------|------------|
| Hamburger/sidenav | Modus navbar has NO shadow DOM (scoped encapsulation); `shadowRoot` is always null; `mainMenuOpenChange` event bubbles and can double-fire | Search light DOM with `navbarWc.querySelector()`, not `shadowRoot.querySelector()`. Fallback must be idempotent `set(open)`, not toggle. See skill section 16 |
| Canvas navbar overflow | Setting `overflow: hidden` clips dropdowns | Static test asserts `overflow: visible`; border-radius on inner element |
| Push-squeeze ordering | Wrong cascade order causes incorrect widget relocation | Unit tests cover right-edge and left-edge squeeze ordering |
| Collision after resize | Active vs relocated widget priority | `_pushSqueezeActive` set tracks active widgets; unit tests cover |
| Widget deselection | Missing `data-widget-id` attribute breaks click-outside | All widget containers must have `[attr.data-widget-id]` |
| Canvas BFS cascade direction | Cascade pusher uses own center for direction, bouncing widgets back toward mover | Direction always references mover center; 16 unit tests in `canvas-push.spec.ts` |
| Canvas detail double rAF | Single rAF reads stale dimensions, pushes incorrectly | Always use double `requestAnimationFrame` before push; see skill section 7 |
| Canvas zoom macOS axis swap | macOS swaps deltaY→deltaX when Shift held; deltaY is 0, zoom direction resolves wrong | Use `Math.abs` comparison of both axes; pick whichever is larger |
| Navbar native rendering (Stencil/Angular 20) | `modus-wc-toolbar` fails to render in dev mode; developers add/remove custom elements creating duplicates in prod or missing elements in dev. Has broken 5+ times. | Runtime detection via `navbarNativeRendered` signal + conditional fallback. All 4 navbar instances must stay in sync. See skill section 23 |
| Shell ng-content in conditional branches | Placing `<ng-content />` inside `@if`/`@else` branches silently destroys projected content. Broke ALL dashboard pages in canvas mode for 2 days (PR #56, Apr 3-5). | Shell must have **exactly 1** `<ng-content />` outside ALL conditional blocks. Static test enforces count and nesting. See skill section 29 |
| Resize twitchiness (`dir='both'`) | Horizontal resize pipeline runs on every frame during vertical-only resize, causing pixel-column round-trip jitter that twitches neighbors | `_hResizeActive` gate: horizontal pipeline only activates after horizontal mouse delta exceeds half a column step. See skill section 32 |
| Widget jumping (collision compaction) | `resolveCollisions` and `compactAll` starting at `y=0` causes distant widgets to teleport upward over intervening widgets | Always start at `tops[id]`; widgets can only move down. See skill section 33 |
| Vercel CDN stale HTML | CDN caches `index.html` for 26+ hours, serving old JS bundles missing new routes | `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate` on HTML responses in `vercel.json` |
| Vercel Angular build cache | `.angular/cache` persists stale route definitions across deploys | `rm -rf .angular/cache` before `npm run build` in `vercel.json` |
| Zone.js context loss (auth callback) | trimble-id library uses axios/CommonJS which exits Zone.js context; post-auth `navigateByUrl` silently fails | Wrap in `NgZone.run()`; add `window.location.replace` hard-redirect fallback |
| Layout seed sharing across personas | Shared "default" seeds meant editing one persona broke others; `exportLayoutSeed()` run with wrong persona overwrote shared file (broke Frank/Bert canvas mode Apr 12-13) | Eliminated ALL shared seeds. 5 personas x 4 pages = 20 independent seed files. 288 static tests in `layout-seeds.spec.ts` enforce file existence, widget lists, no-contamination, geometry, per-persona routing, and export map. See skill section 37 |
| Deepgram master-key role (silent 403) | Read-only / project-scoped keys silently 403 on `auth/grant`; mic appears to do nothing | Master key on Deepgram project must be **Member** or higher. 1-line curl smoke test on `/api/deepgram-token` catches it instantly. See skill section 45 |
| Edge Function endpoints without dev-proxy parity | `npm start` 404s the endpoint; works in production only | Every `api/<name>.ts` must have a matching handler in `dev-proxy.mjs` routed at `localhost:3001`. See skill section 45 |
| `@deepgram/sdk` v5 ConnectArgs booleans | `tsc` accepts `true`/`false`; `ng build` template type-check refuses (`Type 'boolean' is not assignable to type 'string'`) | Use `'true'`/`'false'` string literals for `interim_results`, `smart_format`, `punctuate`. Static test enforces. See skill section 45 |
| Card-on-card invisibility (Modus 1.5) | After `--card` re-pointed to `base-page`, any new `bg-card` cell nested inside another `bg-card` container disappears (page-bg on page-bg with no border between them) | New nested cells must use `bg-muted` (`base-200`) per Modus child-card guidance. Reserve `bg-card` for top-level surfaces paired with `border-default`. See skill section 46 |
| `pdfjs-dist` v5 RenderParameters | v5 makes `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement \| null` a required field on `RenderParameters` (previously inferred from `canvasContext.canvas`). Inline literal call `page.render({ canvasContext, viewport })` fails with TS2345 on v5 (Vercel) but passes on v4 (local) — easy to miss in local dev. | Pass `canvas` through, assigned via a typed local + `as Parameters<typeof page.render>[0]` cast so the call compiles on both v4 and v5. Pattern in `src/app/shared/detail/pdf-viewer.component.ts:301-303`. See PR #129 |
| Widget header drift (inline vs `app-widget-frame`) | RESOLVED May 28, 2026: full refactor migrated all 20 inline-header widgets (5 home, 13 financials, 2 projects-page) onto `app-widget-frame`. Phase 0 extended widget-frame with `titleHierarchy`, optional `icon`, `backButtonAriaLabel` + `backClick`, `headerBelow` slot, `footer` slot, `overflowVisible`, `insightPadding`, `dragHandleSize`. Static test `tests/static/widget-frame-enforcement.spec.ts` now scans every `.ts`/`.html` under `src/app` (excluding demos/dev) and fails if `cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing` appears anywhere outside `widget-frame.component.ts`. | Reach for the appropriate widget-frame input or slot when adding new widgets or modifying existing chrome — never duplicate the header markup inline. If a new requirement genuinely cannot fit through the existing API, extend widget-frame first (and update the test exemption only as a last resort). |
| pdfjs-dist CDN version drift (worker vs API major mismatch) | Pinning a literal `pdfjs-dist@X.Y.Z` on the jsdelivr URL in `pdf-viewer.component.ts` drifts the moment Dependabot bumps the npm dep. PDF.js refuses to render when worker and API are on different majors, and the failure is **silent** — viewer shows only its loading spinner. Broke every drawing in every view (home widget, project Drawings page, canvas detail) for ~2 days after the v4→v5 bump in PR #129. Fixed by PR #133 May 28. | Build the CDN URL from `pdfjsLib.version` so it tracks the installed semver automatically: `const cdn = \`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pdfjs-dist@${pdfjsLib.version}\`;`. Static test `tests/static/pdf-viewer-cdn-version.spec.ts` blocks any hard-coded `pdfjs-dist@\d+\.\d+\.\d+` literal AND requires the `${pdfjsLib.version}` interpolation AND that both worker + cmap paths share the versioned base. |
| Missing `suggestionsProvider` on page-level AI context | Pages that register `contextProvider` + `localResponder` with `AiPageContextService` but no `suggestionsProvider` silently fall back to the controller's page-default agent (e.g. `financialsDefault` / `projectsDefault`) and show generic mixed-topic prompts even when a more specific agent is active (e.g. change-orders subpage shows budget/revenue prompts; selected project tile shows portfolio prompts). Bit financials-page and projects-page before PR #133 May 28. | Whenever a page wires `contextProvider`, also wire `suggestionsProvider` through the **same** agent resolution. The contract is convention-only (no static test) — easy to miss when adding a new page. |
| Cursor/VS Code npm task detector + shell operators in `scripts.*` values | Cursor's NPM task detector emits "Npm task detection: failed to parse the file …/package.json" into the `tasks.workspaceId-…` output channel on every startup when any script value contains a bare shell operator (`\|\|`, `&&`, `;`, `\|`) outside of an `npm exec` / `--` wrapper. The JSON itself parses fine (Node `JSON.parse` ok, `jsonc-parser.parseTree` + `visit` walk cleanly with zero errors), so the failure is in the detector's downstream script-value tokenizer, not the JSON parser. The original Jun 26 fix (embedded `\"` removal in `start` via `concurrently npm:<script>` shorthand) did NOT silence the error — it kept firing for 10+ startups across 5 weeks (logs back to May 26). Real culprit identified Jun 29 via a `jsonc-parser` probe replicating the extension's `readScripts` visitor: only `"prepare": "husky \|\| true"` flagged `SHELL_OP`. The IDE-side dev server still works from a terminal; only the IDE Tasks palette / output-channel hygiene is affected. | Extract any script value containing a shell operator to its own node helper (e.g. `scripts/prepare.mjs` that runs `spawnSync('husky')` and always exits 0 to preserve the `\|\| true` "best effort" semantic). Reference it as `"prepare": "node scripts/prepare.mjs"`. No bare shell operators in any `scripts.*` value. The `concurrently npm:<script>` shorthand from Jun 26 is fine (no shell operators) — keep it. |

